      "title": "feat: Add support for Garmin Connect IQ complication app",
      "body": "Users can now display Trio data on any Garmin watchface that supports Connect IQ complications. This adds a dedicated \"Complication\" app entry that publishes glucose, IOB, COB, and sensitivity ratio data to complication slots. The app itself consumes historical glucose data for its internal 2-hour graph.\r\n\r\n| Garmin App Setting | App & Graph | Watch Complications |\r\n| -- | -- | -- |\r\n| <img width=\"291\" height=\"379\" alt=\"Bildschirmfoto 2026-08-02 um 15 15 50\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3a6ddf15-25a6-4153-8adb-7eab11062337\" /> | <img width=\"408\" height=\"408\" alt=\"CIQ-CoverImage\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a80d1f1-4328-462c-b667-d257f3fb5ef6\" /> | <img width=\"160\" height=\"160\" alt=\"Screen2\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/05c0dc55-82d2-4952-89da-b85ac1697afb\" /> |\r\n\r\nTrio Complication will be available on [Garmin Connect IQ store](https://apps.garmin.com/developer/eae8d754-7a90-4cc7-85f1-95d12ea93490/apps). It's in review with Garmin, once it appears there one necessary condition is achieved for merging PR.",
